course: dictionary
lesson: 3930
title: Feeling frustrated
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Frustrated describes how you feel when you try hard but still cannot do something or get what you want. «I am frustrated because the puzzle will not fit.» The clue is the puzzle will not fit, even though the child keeps trying.
explain: Feeling frustrated is normal when something is hard. «When you get frustrated in practice, break the skill into small steps; small steps lead to big improvement.» You can take a break, breathe slowly, ask for help and try again.
explain: Frustrated can also be a verb, meaning to stop someone's plans from working. «The rain frustrated our plans.» Here the rain did the stopping, so our plans could not go ahead.
fact: Frustrated means upset and annoyed because you cannot do or get something, even though you try.
fact: As a verb, frustrated means stopped someone's plans from working, as in «The rain frustrated our plans».
fact: When you feel frustrated, you can take a break, breathe slowly, ask for help and try again.
fact: Useful phrases: «frustrated with», «frustrated at», «frustrated by», «get frustrated» and «feel frustrated».
fact: A spotted hyena's giggle usually means it is nervous, excited or frustrated, not happy.
exercise: «I am frustrated because the puzzle will not fit.» What does frustrated mean here? | Tired after a long walk | *Upset and annoyed because you cannot make it work, even though you try | Very happy and proud of the puzzle | Lost in the woods
exercise: «The rain frustrated our plans.» What does frustrated mean in this sentence? | Helped our plans go well | *Stopped our plans from working | Made our plans bigger | Took a photo of our plans
exercise: Ruby feels frustrated with her maths sums. What is a good thing for her to do? | Give up and never try again | Tear up her homework | Shout at everyone around her | *Take a break, breathe slowly, then ask for help and try again
test: The hyena's giggle «usually means it is nervous, excited or frustrated, not happy». What does the giggle usually NOT mean? | *Happy | Excited | Nervous | Frustrated
test: Which sentence uses frustrated correctly? | Frustrated the cat is sleeping on the mat | *She got frustrated with the hard puzzle | The frustrated moon sang loudly to the stars | The bus was frustrated by the sunny day
exam: «Putting a name on a feeling helps you calm down and tell someone what you need.» Why does naming a feeling help? | It makes the feeling go away at once | *It helps you understand the feeling, so you can calm down and ask for what you need | It makes the puzzle easier | It means you will never feel frustrated again
